The only difference between the two code snippets is in the handling of the `REGULA_FALSI` method. In the first code snippet, the `f0` value is halved when the method is `ILLINOIS`. In the second code snippet, the `f0` value is updated differently based on the method:
- `ILLINOIS`: Halve the `f0` value.
- `PEGASUS`: Multiply `f0` by `f1 / (f1 + fx)`.
- `REGULA_FALSI`: Adjust the `x0` value to ensure the interval remains within the accuracies.
