### Instruction:
I am trying to understand how to use a custom font in my application. 

Can anyone guide me through this process? I'm using Android Studio and Java as programming language.

Thanks for your time.


A: You can add the following code into your styles.xml file to set a custom font globally:
```java
<style name="AppBaseTheme" parent="android:Theme.Light">
    <item name="android:textViewStyle">@style/MyTextViewStyle</item>
    // other items...
</style>

<style name="MyTextViewStyle" parent="@android:style/TextAppearance.Medium">
    <item name="android:fontFamily">@font/your_custom_font</item>
</style>
```
Then, in your layout XML files you can use the custom font like this:
```java
<TextView
    android:layout_width="wrap_content"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    style="@style/MyTextViewStyle" />
```
Remember to add your custom font file (e.g., Raleway-Regular.ttf) into the res/font directory of your project and declare it in your project's build.gradle file:
```java
android {
    //...

    sourceSets {
        main {
            res.srcDirs = ['src/main/res', 'src/main/fonts']
        }
    }
}
```
And then add this line into your build.gradle file:
```java
android {
    //...

    defaultConfig {
        //...
        
        vectorDrawables.useSupportLibrary = true
    }
    
    //...
}
```
Finally, sync your project and you should be good to go.

Note that the font file name must match exactly with what's declared in styles.xml (e.g., "your_custom_font" instead of "Raleway-Regular.ttf"). 

Also note that not all versions of Android support custom fonts, so you may need to use a library like Calligraphy or RobotoTextView if your target is below API level 23.

If the above steps do not work for you, try cleaning and rebuilding your project. If it still does not work, check that the font file is correctly added into the res/font directory of your project.

